Keep all mutable Super-Rogue state under the directory that the srogue
launcher exports as HOME and ROGUEHOME.  Upstream places its score file in
the first existing host-wide directory among /var/games/roguelike,
/var/lib/roguelike, /var/roguelike, /usr/games/lib and /games/roguelik
whenever ROGUEHOME is unset or missing, and in the working directory when
none exists; use ROGUEHOME, then HOME, instead.  Listing scores with -s now
only reads the score file rather than creating it.

Reject a HOME too long for the game's 80-byte home[] buffer, which upstream
fills with an unbounded strcpy, leaving room for the "/srogue.sav" suffix.
Also bound the copy of the last message into its 80-byte buffer, which a
save prompt naming a long state directory could overflow, and refuse to
restore a save path longer than the 256-byte file_name[] buffer.

Saves store long values as 4 bytes, but rs_read_long and rs_read_ulong
read them into the low half of a long and returned its uninitialized upper
half as well on LP64 systems, so a restored game showed garbage experience
points and could inherit stray creature flags.  Read them as 4-byte
integers instead.

